🧩 FIXED-LENGTH SLIDING WINDOW (Clear & Mechanical)
🔑 Big difference from variable-length
Window size is given and NEVER changes
So:
right moves forward
left moves forward every time window exceeds size K

No “while vs if” confusion here
🧠 Fixed-length sliding window template (MEMORIZE)
int left = 0;
for (int right = 0; right < n; right++) {

    // add right element to window

    if (right - left + 1 > k) {
        // remove left element
        left++;
    }

    if (right - left + 1 == k) {
        // process window
    }
}
This template works for 90% of fixed-window problems.

✅ Problem 1: Maximum sum of subarray of size K
Example
arr = [2,1,5,1,3,2], k = 3
Output = 9   // [5,1,3]

Step 1️⃣ Rule
Window size must be exactly K

Step 2️⃣ What do we track?
Sum of window

Step 3️⃣ Code
int[] arr = {2, 1, 5, 1, 3, 2};
int k = 3;
int left = 0, sum = 0, maxSum = 0;
for (int right = 0; right < arr.length; right++) {
    sum += arr[right];

    if (right - left + 1 > k) {
        sum -= arr[left];
        left++;
    }

    if (right - left + 1 == k) {
        maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, sum);
    }
}
System.out.println(maxSum);

🧠 Why this is easy
    Window size controls movement
    No rule checking
    No frequency map

✅ Problem 2: First negative number in every window of size K
Example
arr = [12,-1,-7,8,-15,30,16,28], k = 3
Output = [-1, -1, -7, -15, -15, 0]

Step 1️⃣ Rule
Window size = K

Step 2️⃣ Data structure
Queue to store negative numbers

Step 3️⃣ Code
int[] arr = {12, -1, -7, 8, -15, 30, 16, 28};
int k = 3;
Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<>();
int left = 0;
for (int right = 0; right < arr.length; right++) {
    if (arr[right] < 0) {
        q.add(arr[right]);
    }

    if (right - left + 1 > k) {
        if (!q.isEmpty() && arr[left] == q.peek()) {
            q.poll();
        }
        left++;
    }

    if (right - left + 1 == k) {
        System.out.print(q.isEmpty() ? 0 : q.peek());
        System.out.print(" ");
    }
}

🧠 Key idea
    Queue tracks useful elements in window
    Remove element when it leaves window

