Why don’t we need a while loop in fixed-length sliding window?
We don’t need a while loop in fixed-length sliding window because the window size is strictly controlled,
and removing exactly one element is always enough to restore the window to size K.

🧠 Why this is true (lock it in your mind)
In fixed-length window:
The only rule is 👉 window size must be K
When size becomes K + 1
❌ window is invalid
✅ removing one element always fixes it
So:
if (windowSize > k) {
    remove one element;
}

There is no scenario where removing one element is not enough — hence no while needed.

🔑 Compare with variable window (quick contrast)
Variable window → rule may still be broken → need while
Fixed window → size violation fixed in one step → if is enough

